  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xe9;ponse multisectorielle et protection en faveur des personnes d&#xe9;plac&#xe9;es de force et retourn&#xe9;es au Niger</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving protection assistance to vulnerable internally displaced people, refugees, returnees and host communities in Diffa, Maradi, Tahoua and Tillabery. This UNHCR project conducts protection monitoring and referrals, reinforces community-based protection mechanisms, provides protection assistance to children and survivors of gender-based violence, and distributes dignity kits. The project provides life-saving assistance to 134,500 people, including 27,000 women, 12,500 men, 95,000 children, and 1,000 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
